primaryEvidenceTexts.4333:
4333 gōśakr̥t n. 'cowdung'. 2. * gōśakara-. [ gṓ-, śákr̥t -] 1. Ash. gasá̃̄ 'cowdung' (→ Tir. gōzā ), K. guhᵃ m.;
S. goho m. 'dried cowdung' (→ Bal. gohāk ), L. g̠ohā m.,
awāṇ. gōˋā ; P. gohā , guhā , gohiā m. 'cowdung', H. gosā m. 2. Sh. (Lor.) gũyoro m. 'a piece of dried cowdung';
P. goerā , goirā m. 'well manured land on the outskirts
of a village'.

