primaryEvidenceTexts.13676:
13676 stabdha 'firmly fixed' ŚvetUp. 2. 'stiff, paralysed,
dull' MBh., 'solidified (as water)' Hariv. [√ stambh ] 1. Pa. thaddha - 'hard, firm'; Pk. thaddha -, thaḍḍha -, thaḍḍhia - 'fixed, firm'; Gy. germ. tardo 'upright';
Shum. tāṛe adv. 'above, up'; K. thodᵘ 'high, erect'; P. ṭhaḍḍā m. 'boundary pillar', ṭhāḍhā 'upright' (← H.);
WPah.jaun. ṭhāṛō 'standing', (Joshi) ṭhāḍā m. 'boundary pillar'; Ku. ṭhāṛo 'upright', m. 'ascent'; N. ṭhāṛo 'upright'; A. thāru 'straight'; B. ṭhāṛa , °ṛā 'upright';
Or. (Sambhalpur) ṭhāḍ 'erect, standing'; Bi. ṭhāṛhab 'to remain, stay'; Mth. ṭhāṛh 'standing erect', ṭhāṛhab 'to stand'; Bhoj. ṭhāṛh 'standing'; OAw. ṭhāḍha 'standing up', pret. 'he stood up', lakh. ṭhāṛh 'standing', ṭhaṛhiyāwab 'to make stand up'; H. ṭhāṛh , ṭhāṛ , ṭhāṛā , ṭhaṛhā 'fixed, stationary, erect, steep', ṭhāṛhnā 'to be fixed, stand up', ṭhaḍḍā m. 'back stick of a
paper kite'; M. ṭhāḍā 'erect'; Si. tada 'firm, hard'. 2. For the development 'firm — sluggish — cold'
cf. * stharati and sthirá- (in H.): Pa. thaddha - 'slow';
Pk. ṭhaḍḍha - 'blunted, cold'; S. thadho 'cold', L. ṭhaḍḍhā , mult. khet. ṭhaḍā ; N. ṭhāṛo 'rude, gauche';
G. tāḍhũ , ṭāḍhũ 'sluggish, contented, cold'. — * thaṇḍha -, * ṭhaṇḍha - infl. by Drav., Tam. taṇ , &c.
'cold' (DED 2473) J. Bloch BSOS v 742 (cf. also Pa. dhandha - 'dull, slow' BHS ii 275): K. thanḍ 'cold', thanḍī f. 'coldness'; Ku. ṭhano 'cold'; N. ṭhā̃ṛo 'abusive name for useless cooking pot' (i.e. 'cold'? But
